  This is part of what makes Barbarians difficult.



  Ranged attacks:  Daggers, as Brian P. advocates, are tough to go wrong
with, especially as Barbs can get to basic skill with them. Elven
daggers don't even need to be foo-proofed.

  Darts are the only possible alternative ranged weapon I can see.
Darts weigh 1/10 as much as daggers and can be poisoned.  There are two
dart traps to #untrap in the VotD.  Save a !oSickness.  

  Mass-bless, mass-poison, mass enchant with max luck and that's ten
times as much ranged damage you can carry around.  That seems less
important since you'll only be throwing one at a time.  You'll be in a
good position to judge for yourself.



  Barbs can get to skilled in attack spells.   A single cast of skilled
cone of cold at XL 15 can do (8 * 9 * 4.5) = 280 points of damage
divided among a 3x3 square.  (Double that for fire-resistant monsters.)
Spell of fireball will do about the same.  Damage from magic missile 
depends solely on XL.  


  Barbs are also about the worst spell casters in the game.  The problem
is you probably won't have enough power.  I doubt it's worth trying even
if you had a robe and the Eye of Aethiopica.  Someone who's tried could
tell you more. 



